  "body": " Reading Quiz 01: Vectors and Kinematics    Contents: This quiz covers sections 1.1 through 1.6, and you may skip material on the cross product.   Instructions: Answer all the questions to the best of your ability on paper. When you are done, screenshot your work and upload it as a pdf using the File Upload question below. When you submit the quiz, don't navigate away from Canvas. Scroll down to the bottom of the page for a download link to the solutions to the quiz.      The geometric sketch of the identity on page 4 seems to assume its result: the vectors and are drawn in different order and different places. What property of vectors allows the sketch to be made as shown and keeps the proof valid?      On page 5, the book shows the projection of on . Draw a sketch of the projection of on and use that to establish the equations for in terms of projections.      On example 1.1, what trig identity is being used to relate and ? Look it up if needed! How are and related?      On page 9, the book writes the equation . It's important to note we won't always use the angle with the x axis. If we defined the angle to be the angle with the y axis, with positive angle defined to be counterclockwise, then what are the components of a vector in terms of and ? Be sure to include a sketch with your answer.     "
