  "body": " Reading Quiz 19: 4-Momentum    Contents: Reading covers sections 8.1 through 8.5.   Instructions: Answer all the questions to the best of your ability on paper. When you are done, screenshot your work and upload it as a pdf using the File Upload question below. When you submit the quiz, don't navigate away from Canvas. Scroll down to the bottom of the page for a download link to the solutions to the quiz.      Conceptually, how is the relativistic energy different from the pre-relativity kinetic energy ? Use the discussion of page 223 as a guide      Briefly explain why the total energy and total momentum for the system of page 224 behaves as a single object with 20 units of mass.      In Chapter 7, we defined the 4-momentum to be (the undertilde is a notation for 4-D vectors, like the arrow over 3-D vectors). Photons are massless particles, so the in the definition of the 4-momentum is a problem. Is there another issue in trying to define the 4-momentum as we did in Chapter 7?      Figure 8-6 shows the solution to a collision of a photon of energy that backscatters off a free electron. Write the conservation of momentum and conservation of energy equations for this collision, keeping the final energy of the photon and the electron as unknowns. There is no need to solve the equations.      The figure in page 234 states that the polyelectron is moving at . Explain this result from the information given in that figure.     "
